That has been my observation too.  There are several alternatives:

- DSP is another DOS program and version 2.12 works (V2.20 doesn't
work).  On the RZ55 there is one vendor-specific mode page.  There a 01
byte and I changed it to 00.  (Look for dsp212.zip)

- I've used both rzdisk and scu under MIPS Ultrix 4.4 on DECstations. 
Both work and they actually know about what's in that modepage, so you
get asked a question instead of having to hex-edit the mode page.

- I've heard that DECstation firmware allows you to change that bit and
that there's even a way to do it with VAXstation firmware.  I have only
observed that the VAXstation 3100 M38 disables spin-up on power-up and I
don't know how to use the firmware to enable it.  If anybody knows how
to do this, I'd like to know.

- Get the SCSI spec and something that allows you to send raw SCSI
commands.  Good luck...

- sformat (Unix utility that runs on a variety of unices) allows you to
do stuff with mode pages.  However I couldn't find how to alter
vendor-specific mode pages with it.

