Robert McConnell (rmcconne.NOSPAM@lightlink.com) wrote:
: Good morning,
: 
: I have been given an LN03+ which I have been able to connect to my
: Linux system and print plain text files. But it has a blank streak in
: columns 77-79, and any attempt to send it files with control sequences
: results in controller errors. The test sheet prints ok with 32 lines
: of fonts, but appears to be printing two lines each of 16 fonts. The
: same blank steak appears on the test sheet.

The blank streak is typically caused by some foreign material in the
development unit (toner hopper).  If you pull out the "drawer" all the way
out, take off the OPC belt and look at the toner hopper where the OPC belt
touches it, you'll see a roller with toner on it.  You'll also see the area on
that roller where there is no toner.  That's the cause of your blank streak.

To resolve it, you'll need a toner vacuum.  Remove the piece that shields the
joint between this development roller (one screw).  Then, above the roller,
there are 3 screws that hold a blade that sits just above the roller.  The
problem is typically that there is some obstruction between this blade and the
roller.  You'll need to take out the blade and vacuum the area out.  Then,
put it all back together again.  Make sure that when you screw down the blade
that it's pushed down as far as it will go against the roller.  It won't
actually touch the roller, but if you don't push it down, it'll allow too much
toner on the roller, spoiling your printouts and fouling the OPC belt.

The controller errors: are the just the lightning bolt and the number 6?  If
so, then that means "thinking".  And, remember that the printer won't appear
to do anything until it receives a form feed.

        Stu



