Everyone is correct about a toner clog,  but you don't have to remove
anything.  Just slowly rotate the large gear on the right side back and
forth the debris will then be exposed.  Also you can take a piece of paper
and place it underneath the blade.  If you lift up on the lever with the
small white roller on it it will move the spring inside the hopper and mix
the toner.  If you still need books let me know.


