:OPENVMS FACT SHEET
:
:   The following is an operating system FACT SHEET on OPENVMS. A Fact Sheet is
:an organized summary of information and complements the more common FAQ
:(Frequently Asked Questions). This Fact Sheet derived from
:<http://www.honeycomb.net/os/oses/vms.htm>. Report any errors, ommissions,
:corrections, additions, etc. to <MerefBast@aol.com>.
..

  Interesting website, there's a lot of information there...

  In no particular order, comments:

  I see no need to continue the confusion over "VMS" and "OpenVMS".
  (The operating system formerly known as "VMS" is now known as 
  "OpenVMS", and it runs on various "VAX" and "Alpha" systems...)

  There were a number of other folks that helped design the VAX
  hardware and the original version of VMS all those years ago, in 
  addition to Dave Cutler and Dick Hustvedt.  Both would recognize 
  it now (were they either able or willing to look at it), but there 
  have been a vast number of changes since either of these two chaps
  last worked on it.

  Machine readable source code listings for the operating system are 
  available, with only a small number of modules are expurgated from 
  the listings distributions.  (This availability differs markedly
  from various other proprietary operating systems.)
  
  The current version is V7.1-2 on OpenVMS Alpha, and V7.1 on OpenVMS 
  VAX.  Per the current schedule, the V7.2 release will be arriving at 
  customer sites early in 1999.

  _Writing Real Programs in DCL_ is now shipping a second edition, by 
  Paul Anagnostopoulos and some other fellow.  (qv http://www.bh.com/)

  As for user group websites, I'd definitely want to include the DECUS 
  website (http://www.decus.org/) in the list.

