In article <368751BE.6243540@writeme.com>, Garfield Cat <garfieldcat@writeme.com> writes:
:  I hit an error while sorting a file about 2xxxx blocks, it said
:insufficient virtual memory. What params should I change to handle the
:error ? 

  Well, I'll assume this question is about OpenVMS, even though it's 
  posted in the generic newsgroup -- comp.os.vms would be a more common 
  spot for OpenVMS questions.  I'll also assume the error message was 
  INSVIRMEM.  (The operating system version and platform, as well as the 
  exact error message, might be interesting -- it would certainly make
  it easier to answer the question with more certainty...)

  The usual suspects are the SYSGEN parameter VIRTUALPAGECNT, and the 
  process quota PGFLQUOTA.  (On OpenVMS Alpha V7.0 and later releases,
  VIRTUALPAGECNT is not particularly interesting.)  Use AUTOGEN and a
  higher MIN_VIRTUALPAGECNT setting to raise the former limit via the
  MODPARAMS.DAT file, and use AUTHORIZE to raise the latter value.

  You may also need to increase the size of the system pagefile(s)
  to account for the new usage, and you might also need to configure
  additional physical memory into the system.

