> From my experience to design some mainframes, it is not so difficult
> to have a large set of TLB entiries. If one use the set associative
> method.

Amen.

Although it should also be noted that, for matrix multiply,
the TLB misses can be done out-of-order, and could be made
to overlap with each other.

The high cost of TLB misses is in large part due to the "stop the world"
implementation. P6 allowed TLB misses to proceed without blocking
independent instructions.  Pipelining TLB misses is an obvious next step.





