In a post I just sent off I mentioned the possibility of
non-blocking and pipelined TLB miss handling.

Such handling could be done by a suitable hardware
state machine page table walker - or by a separate thread.

It may be worth emphasizing that non-blocking and pipelined
TLB miss handling may be most useful hiding the latency
of L1 TLB misses that hit in an L2 TLB --- thus avoiding
the extremely large latencies that might be associated with
walking page tables in memory.

And, by the way...  I hope nobody throws up the "TLB misses
must use uncached memory accesses" red herring. That has been
proven wrong long back.





