Have seen a similar situation with an AlphaServer 1000a system.  SCSI bus
was modified (unterminated, then a tape drive added, then re-terminated)
while the system was up.  Blew out the on-motherboard SCSI controller.  Bad
Bad thing to have happen...motherboards are expensive to replace.

