CaptMac44 <captmac44@aol.com> wrote in message
news:19981229145834.00806.00003575@ng-fv1.aol.com...
>I have a 3/4" blank border around my screen.  I can't seem to get the
desktop
>or any file to fill the entire screen.  Any suggestions?

You don't say which model HiNote you have, but this answer applies to most
of them.

Unlike a CRT, an LCD laptop display has discrete pixels.  Unless the BIOS
supports an "expansion" mode (which more often than not just blurs the
picture), if your display adapter resolution is set to a lower resolution
than the screen has, you'll only illuminate a subset of the pixels.

Most HiNotes have 800x600 resolution, and I would guess you have your
display set to 640x480.  Go into the Display settings and change the
resolution to 800x600.  If it doesn't let you, make sure that the "monitor
type" is set to an 800x600 LCD display.


