An RA7x is a large house brick sized SDI drive. Roughly the same size/weight
as an RD54.
An SA70 storage adapter holds 4 RA7x drives, and would no doubt be lighter,
quieter, less power hungry and cooler than any single RA8x drive.
RA70's are 250mb
RA71 is ~800Mb (I think)
RA72 is 1Gb
RA73 is 2Gb.


I wasn't even aware there were SDI controllers for MVII's!   What's the part
number/name of
the device?   I have several RA70's that I could use instead of RD54's in my
MVII if I can get hold
of one of these....:^).

You learn something every day.....

