martin@RADIOGAGA.HARZ.DE (Martin Vorlaender) writes:

> Frank Samuelson (fwsam@nospam.iastate.edu) wrote:
> : I have an iso-9660 CD image on my SCSI drive.  I would like to be 
> : able to mount and read this image as a file system.

>   # mount -t cdfs /dev/rz?c /mount-point

> (? being the SCSI id of the drive)

This will just mount a disk at /mount-point, expecting a cdfs file
system.  I believe the poster wanted a loop device mount, like linux'

	mount -o loop,ro /path/to/file.iso /mount-point

mounting an ISO image in a regular file as if it were a block device
with an ISO file system on it.  If DU doesn't support it natively, the 
simplest way might be to boot a PC with Linux, NFS export the volume
containing the ISO image, mount with loop the image on the Linux box,
and NFS import it back on the DU machine. :-)

~kzm
