Paul Repacholi wrote:
>Antonio Carlini (carlini@marvin.reo.dec.com) wrote:
>In article <756qrt$go7$1@newsreader5.core.theplanet.net>, "Graham >>Godfrey" <graham@vbuster.demon.co.uk> wrote:
>>>And don't forget it is not Y2K compliant.

>>In what way? If it isn't compliant it's news both to me and the one I
>>run in the lab! It probably hasn't been tested so it may well be
>>labelled on some web  page as "we don't know - don't call us" 
>>but I am not aware of any Y2K problem. 

> RSX on the console? Is there an update for y2k for that?

VENUS-based VAXen (8600's) run a variant of RT-11 on the console
processor.

8500, 8700, and 88x0 VAXen run a highly-customized POS, descended 
from RSX-11M+, on the console PRO 380.

Recent RT-11 and RSX-11M+ versions are Y2K compliant (see
http://www.mentec.com/), but evidently DEC doesn't have the
resources to devote to upgrading the console subsystems
of the above-mentioned systems.  To quote from
  
  http://ww1.digital.com/year2000/position.asp:

 The PRO380 operating system uses only 2-digit years, and will show the
 Year 2000 as "00". There are no plans to modify the PRO380 code to be
 Year 2000 Ready. 

 On VAX 8600 systems, the PDP-11 console uses an operating system
 based on an RT-11 version that is not Year 2000 
 Ready; there are no plans to update the console to a newer RT-11
 version. 

