In article <75n4f2$pgu$1@news.mel.aone.net.au>, "Geoff Roberts" 
<geoffrobx@stmarksx.ppx.catholicx.edux.aux> wrote:

>I wasn't even aware there were SDI controllers for MVII's!   What's the part
>number/name of
>the device?   I have several RA70's that I could use instead of RD54's in my
>MVII if I can get hold
>of one of these....:^).

The device you want is a KDA50, this is the Q-bus equivalent of the VAXBI 
KDB50. It is a two board set and chews up a fair bit of power. I have two 
BA23-based uVAX IIs that talk to RA7x disks. You will need the KDA50, internal 
cables and an appropriate bulkhead mounting (sufficient for two drives on a 
BA23 - you need two mountings to talk to all four possible RA devices). Then 
you cable up your BA23 to whatever external enclosure your RA devices live in. 

You may be able to mount an RA70 in the BA23 and go directly to the RA drive 
from the KDA50 (any odd number of SDI cables works - this is how BA213 boxes 
are wired to take internal RA drives). If you go this route you need to work 
out how to tell the RA drive its unit number and whether it is write protected 
etc. since there will be no OCP to do that for you.

Antonio

