David Lucas <davidl@centuryinteractive.com> writes:
> I purchased an alphastation 200 from webauction.com.  They have been
> selling for about $200.  It came without a hard drive, cdrom, video card
> nor update utility.  I bought an update utility from Digital.  I have a
> SCSI cdrom, won't work.  It does not use 512 byte blocks.  Borrowed a
> Toshiba Cdrom from work.  It worked to load the utility.  Bought a PCI
> video card, it seems to work.  I bought a 9.1gig SCA SCSI hard drive.
> OOPS!..

  Must have been one of the later ones. The earlier ones came with video
cards. I don't know if generic video cards are supported under NT - under
VMS you need one of the DEC cards (some of which are built by DEC and some
of which are OEM'd - some of my systems came with #9 330 cards and some
came with DEC cards of various flavors).

  If by "update utility" you mean the console firmware, it's downloadable
for free from DEC: ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware

> IS THIS A PROBLEM????  Will the alphastation 200 run NT server or only
> workstation?  I can not get either to load.  I have tried partitioning
> the hard drive various ways.  None seem to work.  When NT starts to load
> it either dies at the scan the hard drive or if I bypass the scan, when
> I start to load.  I get a blue screen with a bunch of trash (to me) on
> it.  It is not an NT blue screen of death, but a DEC screen.  Once ARC
> is loaded, is there a way to make it stay instead of going back to SRM?
> help pleeeeease

  You might want to post the "bunch of trash" and see if it makes sense to
anyone else.

  Most of these systems only came with 16MB or 32MB of memory in 'em - you
need a *LOT* more memory to run NT. A friend of mine is running NT (server,
I think) on one of these and he's bumped it up to over 100MB.

  Regarding ARC/SRM, I don't know what you mean by "make it stay" - there
isn't enough flash in these boxes as shipped to hold both the ARC and SRM
firmware (though you can add two PLCC flash chips), so the firmware updater
should ask you which one you want to install, and it should stay put until
you re-flash.

