I have a 2Gb Seagate Barracuda (RZ28-alike) in my 4000/60.  While Seagate's
specs indicate this a slightly cooler running drive anyway, I find it runs
at what feels like a perfectly normal temperature.  Given that these drives
don't have the best reputation in the PC world, I would say this speaks well
of the excellent enclosure design of the 4000 - the drives sit right next to
one of the cooling fans, in a free-flowing air space.

