> *do* they use? "virtual address space" sounds a little too generic
> to me.

If a particular cross-platform application like Oracle uses a term,
that does _not_ mean it is in general use by VMS folk.  I have used
VMS for 20 years and have only read this acronym in this discussion.

Also, "Oracle" is a fuzzy term.  There are two Oracle product lines
on VMS, and Oracle Rdb presumably uses the same terms it used when
DEC developed it.  Since Oracle Rdb is quite cluster-friendly, I
would not be surprised if it were more popular on VMS than the
cross-platform Oracle.

Larry Kilgallen



