Sue,

The Digital PC 5510 comes with two CDs: Windows 95 (or NT depending on
which version that you order) and the Restore CD. All of the correct drivers

for video (there are two types of video that can be ordered on the 5510 -
integrated Matrox Mystique or add-on Diamond AGP), sound (the sound chip
is a Crystal 4236B), and network are found on the Restore CD.

Inserting the restore CD will auto-start the restore program. From there you

should be able to install the correct drivers.

Under NT, you should be installing from the NT 4.0 CD and also installing
the
Service Pack 3 (install the SP3 before you install the video drivers).

You can also go to the Matrox home page and get the latest drivers for the
Mystique.
If you have the Diamond AGP video, you can get the latest drivers from their

home page. You can tell which video you have installed by where the video
cable plugs in:

-- if it plugs into a connector on the mother board (the board with the
keyboard and
mouse connectors) then that's the integrated Matrox

-- if the cable plugs in to a connector that appears to be separate, then
that's the AGP.

regards,

glen kelley
compaq

