I have two stupid and unrelated questions concerning the Digital
Alpha PWS500au Unix systems.

1) I can use xcd to play an audio CD on the system and it works
fine if I use headphones, but if I use the internal speaker on
the workstation then the volume is VERY LOW even with the xcd
volume setting turned to maximum. Is there a way to increase
the internal volume speaker?  While I'm on the subject of the
internal speaker, is there a way to change either the volume or
pitch of the obnoxious beep in X11? It is really annoying. Using
"xset b" doesn't seem to have any effect on volume except for
"xset b off" turns it off completely.


2) I need to connect an HP7550 pen plotter to one of the serial
ports on this workstation and am having trouble doing it through
the use of lpr and printcap. We had no trouble doing this with
our old Dec Ultrix workstations (mips based). Below is the printcap
entry we used on that system. But on the Alpha system the plotter
spits out a page but does no printing and the plotter's lcd display
shows that there was a transmission error.

plotter1|hp1|hp7550|7550|HP7550 8-pen auto-feed plotter:\
        :lp=/dev/tty01:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/plotter1d:\
        :br#9600:\
        :fc#0177477:\
        :ff=PG;:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lpd-errs:\
        :of=/usr/local/bin/hp7550f:\
        :sh:\
        :rs:

and the output filter mentioned above (hp7550f) was a very
simple program:


#include     <stdio.h>
#include     <sgtty.h>

#define BUFSIZE (1024)

main(argc, argv)
    int argc;
    char **argv;
{

    hp7550_init();
    hp7550_cat();
    exit(0);
}

hp7550_init()
{   struct sgttyb params;
    extern int errno;

    if (ioctl(fileno(stdout), TIOCGETP, &params) == -1) {
	fprintf(stderr, "hp7550f ioctl get failed %d\n", errno);
    }
    params.sg_flags &= ~(ECHO|XTABS|CRMOD);
    params.sg_ospeed = params.sg_ispeed = B9600;
    if (ioctl(fileno(stdout), TIOCSETP, &params) == -1) {
	fprintf(stderr, "hp7550f ioctl set failed %d\n", errno);
    }
}

hp7550_cat()
{   char c[BUFSIZE];
    int got;

    while ((got = read(fileno(stdin), c , BUFSIZE)) > 0) {
	write(fileno(stdout), c, got);
    }
}

