David Mason Curry wrote:
> 
> Are SCSIA and SCSIB really just the e same thing, or are there two SCSI
> controllers in a VAXstation 3100 (m38 for me)?  I am confused because
> the documention indicates that I can only have 7 SCSI devices when I
> expected to be able to connect 14 with two seperate buses.

A typical M38 has two SCSI host adapters, one for internal
drives and one for external drives.  Internally there's only space
for two SCSI devices, but externally you can have up to 7.  If
you're clever you'll find some way of bringing the internal bus
to the outside world.

Depending on the exact lineage of your M38, you might have just
1 SCSI host adapter serving both internal and external devices.
But most shipped with two.

Tim.



