Indeed there is a tradeoff. The TurboLaser Senior (8400) has a nine-slot
backplane. Since you have to have at least CPU board (2 CPUS), one
memory board, and one I/O board, you have six slots left to play with.
Accordingly, you can have:

14 CPUS, one 1/O board, one memory board
28GB of memory, two CPUs, one I/O board
More PCI channels than you shake a stick at, plus two CPUs and one
memory board.

Or a mixture of the above. Clearly not the most balanced system on the
planet.

