> Cameron Laird           http://starbase.neosoft.com/~claird/home.html
> claird@NeoSoft.com      +1 281 996 8546 FAX


Well, the 2nd is what my DU 4.0 host has.  The first is really puzzling,
since there seems to be no advantage to having /dev/null executable.  I
changed the perms on my /dev/null to 777 & tried executing it & the
response back is:
/dev/null: not found.

Not having write permission for normal users, though, probably would
cause all types of errors with scripts.  The group & perms being changed
obviously points to the change being made as root.  You might want to
check your backups to see when the change was made.



