In article <74s2rn$bmi$1@nnrp1.dejanews.com>, weebuwaabu@hotmail.com wrote:
>have been hard on them. The II is obviously a parts machine, the (for lack of
>a proper term) main computer box was just sorta sitting in the rolling rack
>frame, crooked, not screwed in. no drive0, just what looks like a DLT tape
>drive. in the bottom of the rack cabinet, there is a drawer with two maxtor
>drives,  says SYSTEM INDUSTRIES on it. No matter waht I do with te station
>II, the little red display starts by saying F, then jumps to A and stays
>there. Run light comes on for a bit and stays off.  Can only get text on my

Test A is checking for a video controller. Look for a QVSS (M7602) or
a QDSS (M7168 & M7169). If you find any try removing them and
replacing them with a grant card - you may also need to change the
jumpers on other modules (it would be useful if you posted a list
of the cards in there).

>it wont boot. Also, when in the >>> promt, it tells me that SHOW CONFIG is an
>invalid command, as are most that I learned from the 4000. Heres a screen of
>startup and all the happens when I try to boot: KA650-B  V1.2/0123

The V1.2 ROMs are pretty early - too old to have much more than the
same commands you will find in a MicroVAX II. If you can get the later
ROMs (V5.3?) then you get most of the commands that you know and
love from you VAX 4000. In particular you get the CONFIG command
which lets you determine the correct CSR/VEC settings for a specified 
configuration.

