:leave it long enough, it wiil retry. So, DUA0 is my first disk, is XQA0 the
:'expansion' disk area or is it the DEQNA ethernet?

  No, DUA0 is simply the device it was set to bootstrap from.  You
  may or may not have a DUA0 device present or functional/bootable.

  KA640, KA650, and later generally have a specified target boot 
  device.  The earliest of the KA650 processors and all KA630 have 
  a "sniffer" bootstrap, a bootstrap that will look for the first 
  bootable device found according to a preset sequence of device 
  checks.  See HELP on the >>> prompt of your VAXstation 3200 for 
  details of the various configuration options available.

  Your KA650 V1.2 PROM version should have HELP and such available
  at the >>> console prompt.

  The MicroVAX II and VAXstation 3200 typically used the RQDX3 disk
  controller with RD54 disks, but other storage combinations were
  available for these systems as well.

:As I understand it, my
:only hope for getting this machine to boot is getting that dflug cd, SOMEHOW
:finding a HSD05 or HSD10 and hooking my SCSI cd rom up that way? Can I somhow
:set up the 4000 to boot up the other machine(s) over the ethernet?

  The KZQSA or the KFQSA DSSI controller and HSDnn DSSI to SCSI adapter
  are how one can connect a CD-ROM drive to the MicroVAX II or the 
  VAXstation 3200, yes.  InfoServer or served access is another option.
  There may well be some third-party approaches as well, but YMMV.

  You can also boot off magtape (typically TK50 in these systems), but 
  you'll need to acquire a bootable tape kit or have somebody set up a 
  bootable TK50 tape kit for you.  (STABACKIT is shipped with OpenVMS,
  and allows the creation of bootable tape media on TK50 and other
  bootable devices.)

