> benchmarks. According to them, all of the major vendors can claim to
> be "top of something".
>
> Compaq leads in TPC-C (clustered), SPECweb, SPECfp95, SPECint95, and
> AIM UNIX workstation.

One has to be very careful with onliner comparisons of SPECweb benchmarks.
The choice of link type can have a profound impact on the resulting number.
Another way of saying it is that using FDDI makes the benchmark "easier" than
using Ethernet flavors with a 1500 byte MTU, and using ATM or Jumbo Frames
makes it easier still.

Some rough idea of the impact can be found by looking at the brief paper at
ftp://ftp.cup.hp.com/dist/networking/briefs/ - the "WebMTU" paper (multiple
formats).

