In article <19981207165944.23333.00003356@ng33.aol.com>, andy3434@aol.com (Andy3434) writes:
:I have just obtained a VAXstation 3100. (Model  VS42A - 80 - i think).  What
:sort of monitor can I use with it?  Sorry I am new to DEC.

  There is no VAXstation 3100 model 80.

  The models available in the VAXstation 3100 series are the models
  30 & 40, the models 38 & 48, and the model 76.

  The KA42-A was used in the models 30 and 40 and the KA42-B was used
  on the 38 and 48.

  If you've got two horizontal rows of louvers on the side of the
  enclosure, it's a 30 or a 38, three rows inicates a 40 or a 48.
  (The only difference between the 30 and 40, or the 38 and the 48,
  is the size of the enclosure, and the internal storage expansion.
  The 4x series is a larger enclosure.)

  The monitors are VR160, VR297, VR299 (GPX graphics) or VRT19
  (SPX graphics) -- the key here is that the monitors must handle
  synch-on-green.

  See the OpenVMS Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) for some information
  on this: "MISC3.  Can I reuse old keyboards, mice and monitors with 
  a PC?", etc.  Archives such as www.dejanews.com should be able to
  find various discussions as well, as there have been a number of
  similar discussions.

  You'll also need to acquire an appropriate cable.  BC23K-03 was
  the color cable, if memory serves.

  Talk to a used-equipment vendor, they should be able to set you up
  with what you need.

