No.  "Digital UNIX" is the same product that "Digital OSF/1" used to be.
Ultrix is a different beast completely.  OSF/1 (a.k.a. Digital UNIX) *never*
ran on the VAX.  Many (all?) of the VAX 4000 systems never ran Ultrix,
because VAX Ultrix was almost dead by the time they were introduced.  So it's
possible there's no Unix at all from DEC that you can run, much less today's
Digital UNIX.

I don't believe NetBSD runs on the 4000/300 -- yet.  It runs on the 4000/60,
and support for other 4000 models is in the works.

