The level of RAS provided by DIGITAL UNIX for a certain class of customer is
sufficient for them, no matter what some report says.

Suppose Solaris stood still for a year or two, and everybody (including
Windows NT) raced ahead of it in all categories. Does that mean that all of
your customers who are currently happy with their Solaris systems will rush
to get rid of them because they now have a low score? Obviously not: your
customers are satisfied with what Solaris provides, no matter where the OS
ranks in some theoretical report.

