I hope that the N is not to big, experience with large N NUMA 
systems show that long off-node latency is a real killer for 
real world performance. One reason why some vendors are now 
using OPS to partion the DBMS within an OS instance.


> > If you can make a task run faster by splitting the OS in two instances
> > on teh same hardware, this really only means one thing: the scalability of
> > the OS sucks.  In other words: there is a software bottleneck in the OS
