  The following is probably more than you ever wanted to know, but...

  HSD05-J* was the HSD05 variant targeted for BA4xx series enclosures,
  installing in certain members of the BA4xx Q-bus enclosures.  (I do 
  not believe this module is presently available for ordering.)

    HSD05-JA  BA430, BA440, B400X, factory installed
    HSD05-JF  BA430, BA440, B400X, field installed
    HSD05-JG  BA441, B401X-A9, factory installed
    HSD05-JH  BA441, B401X-A9, field installed

  The HSD05-J* module was found on (or was optional on) various of the
  DSSI VAX 4000 Q-bus systems that shipped after the retirement of the 
  DSSI storage widgets.

  The HSD05-J* does *not* use the Q-bus for communications, though it
  does occupy one Q-bus slot -- it connects to a DSSI bus originating
  on an adapter located elsewhere in the system, converting it to SCSI.
  The following adapters were supported on the same DSSI bus:

    EDA670  VAX 4000 Internal DSSI 
    D4000   DEC 4000 Internal DSSI 
    KFDDA   VAX 4000-100 DSSI Option
    KFDDB   VAX 4000-5/6/700 DSSI Option
    KFMSA   XMI to DSSI 
    KFQSA   Q-bus to DSSI 

  Various of the supported SCSI disks behind the adapter are generally 
  identified as RF72 DIAn: widgets, while the supported SCSI tapes will
  show up as TU81 MUAn: devices.

  The SCSI bus behind the HSD05-J* is limited to the storage bays internal 
  to the BA440 or BA430 enclosure.

  There are a few other (relatively minor) configuration restrictions.

  Some of the related documentation:

    EK-HSDD5-IN  "DSSI-SCSI Install VAX4000"
    EK-HSDC5-IN  "HSD05 DSSI-SCSI Op Info BA400"
    EK-BA44A-IN  "BA400 Series Devices Install"
    EK-RRDDD-IN  "RRD43 CD-ROM Operations Guide"


