> I just purchased an Alphastation 200, and need the firmware update CD for
> it.  I need to change from the SRM console to the ARC console, and
> understand that this CD is necessary to perform that procedure.
>

Nope, not necessary.  If you have a PC you can:

   1. Get the mkboot.exe file from
           ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/digital/Alpha/firmware/utilities/
      ( read the mkboot.txt while you are there )

   2. Get the latest firmware upgrade file from
           ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/digital/Alpha/firmware/v5.3/alpha200/

   3. On your PC, use mkboot to create a bootable floppy using mkboot
           mkboot as200_v6_9.exe

   4. On your AlphaStation get inside the box and find the jumper that
      allows you to boot floppy instead of flashROM ( J2 ).
      Jumper pins 2-3

   5. Startup the AlphaStation with the floppy and follow the firmware
        upgrade instructions



