> discount store than you would pay for _any_ manufacturer's CPU
> cabinet.

I think Solaris can do this now (e.g. when partitioning an E10K) and
I'm sure Wildfire will be able to. Just ask the memory controller to
kindly swap out all the pages in board N to disk and then replace
it. No problem. I realise this is a simplification but I don't see a
major hurdle. There may be some memory which isn't used for the
virtual memory pages but in that case it's likely to be small so why
not use hardware redundancy or perhaps just more reliable types of
memory.

