See http://www.ideasinternational.com/benchmark/bench.html, a good
one-stop shopping source for who's currently at the top of the major
benchmarks. According to them, all of the major vendors can claim to
be "top of something".

Compaq leads in TPC-C (clustered), SPECweb, SPECfp95, SPECint95, and
AIM UNIX workstation.

Sun leads in TPC-D power (30 GB and 1 TB databases), SAP S&D, and
SAP C/S.

SGI leads in SPECint_rate95, OPC ViewPerf, AIM UNIX fileserver, and
AIM UNIX shared app server.

IBM leads in SPECfp_rate95, TPC-D power (100 GB), and parallel SAP.

I wasn't trying to dispute your facts or to argue for Sun vs. Compaq.
I simply wanted to point out that the thread was becoming irrelevant
to most comp.os.vms readers - and that a more OS-neutral group like
comp.os.vms seemed like an appropriate forum for continuing the
