Howard Bangerter wrote:
> 
> I have a 5.25 floppy written by a Pro350 (RX51 drive?) many years ago.
> I now don't have access to a Pro350 any more, and am wondering if there
> is any way to get these files (text) converted to a current format (DOS,
> etc.).  Anyone out there who can help me?

If the operating system you were using on the Pro was RT-11, it's
readable on a 5.25" HD drive on a PC-clone using John Wilson's
PUTR ( ftp://ftp.dbit.com/putr/ ).  Also readable on any VAX/VMS
machine with RX50 floppies, or any PDP-11 under RSX or RT
with RX50 drives.

If it was done under POS, any RSX-11 or VMS machine will be able
to mount the ODS-1 filesystem.  Then it's a simple matter of
FTP'ing the files to where you want them.

Another operating system that ran on the Pro was VENIX.

If you don't want to seek out any of the above resources on your
own, I (and others) provide such media conversions as a commercial
service.

