I have setup a Web page relative to sound on OpenVMS workstations, but the
freewares I've ported to OpenVMS are generally also available for DU. I think
it's worth to take a look at Mpeg audio Layer 3 encoding for your need. You
can record your vinyls at 32 khz or 44.1 khz sample rate on your DU
workstation, and create your mp3 files with the ISO/MPEG Dist 10 codec. You
play with mpg123, a fast and high quality mpeg audio player available for DU
and VMS (and other Unixes). My web page is at url:

  http://www2.cenaath.cena.dgac.fr/~pmoreau/audio/mpeggb.html

An Mpeg audio layer 3 files needs about 1 Mbyte for 1 minute of stereo CD
quality music (12 Mbytes in raw CD PCM format). If you are interested in MIDI,
you can take a look at url:

  http://www2.cenaath.cenaath.cena.dgac.fr/~pmoreau/audio/midigb.html

Patrick

