Check DejaNews for recent posts either in comp.sys.dec or comp.os.vms - the
answer is to briefly short together two solder pads which are located right
next to the Dallas clock chip.  This resets the NVRAM to, presumably, factory
settings, so you'll need to re-establish boot devices, keyboard language, etc,
and re-supply the date when VMS boots.

