Tsunami supports 2 CPUs, each on a 64 bit bus at up to 333Mhz.  So,

64x333e6/8 = 2.664GB/s

x2 = 5.328 GB/s

Tsunami supports up to 2 256bit 83Mhz memory busses. So,

256 *83e6 = 2.656GB/s

x2 = 5.312 GB/s


In the max tweek config it does hit >5.2 peak.  Sustained will of
course be lower.  But I still think that the bandwidth difference
between Sun's UE6xxx and the dual processor EV6 will be small.  So,
lets see, up to 24 processors with ~2GB(I'm giving Sun some extra
performance here) versus a 2 processor machine...  Damn sun has poor
balance.  To bad they have HIGH latency in the machine with the big
bandwidth numbers.  I'm still waiting on a TPC number... 



