re: hot swapping of memory

Tandem's architecture on oder boxes such as Cyclones requires "fault tolerant
software" and 
system setup. (just because it runs on a Tandem does not make a program fault tolerant).

Typically, a program would run on 2 CPUs in a Tandem. So you could shut down a
CPU and memory and have the program continue to run on the alternate
CPU/memory as you swapped components.

But if you configured an application to run only on a single CPU, you couln't
shut down that CPU or swap memory without affecting that process/program.



