In article <36691a95.11246936@news.asn-linz.ac.at>, Hans.Bachner@altavista.net (Hans Bachner) writes:
:Or check whether it has a SCSI adapter (KZQSA, was mentioned further
:down) which would allow you to use SCSI disks as well - you'd probably
:need to be creative to get them mounted somehow in the box without the
:"official" adapters.

  The KZQSA is supported only CD-ROM devices and SCSI tapes.

  The KZQSA adapter does not support standard SCSI magnetic disks.
  Some folks have tried it with certain magnetic disks and it has 
  seemed to work for them, and various other folks have had problems.  
  I do not recommend the configuration.  (The Systems and Options
  Catalog has generally included this restriction, and the OpenVMS
  V7.2 SPD now also includes this restriction.)

  The typical solution is an HSD05 or HSD10 controller -- the HSD 
  series adapters allow various SCSI disks to be connected to a DSSI 
  bus.  Certain of the HSD05 controllers reside directly in the Q-bus 
  packplane (for power and mounting), while others in the HSD series
  reside in the StorageWorks enclosure.

