This isn't entirely the case, as far as my experience.  We have several
600au's, and before that spent a few months demo-ing a 600a running NT. 
When we decided we wanted to look at the 600au, the field sales/marketing
technical rep for Digital showed up with a seperate hard disk (preloaded
with Digital UNIX) and changed a few settings inside the AlphaBIOS firmware
and was able to access SRM and boot right up (basically changed a few things
and brought it right up as a 600au).

We later tried this on a 433a one of our admin's bought used, and had no
difficulties on this end.  We did, however, end up having problems when we
realized that his 433a used an Adaptec SCSI controller, as opposed to the
QLogic-based Digital controller supported by Digital UNIX.

In a nutshell, yes, you should be able to switch your 500a over to run UNIX
or VMS.


: >Ok, but what's to stop someone downloading the SRM console firware from
