helbig@man.ac.uk (Phillip Helbig) writes:

>I've heard that some really old ethernet controllers, like in QBUS 
>machines, are not supported (and it really doesn't always work) for 
>clustering with newer versions of VMS.

>Is it possible that anytime in the foreseeable future (say, 3 years:)
>other, older ethernet controllers---like on older SCSI
>VAXstations---might not work if in a cluster with a modern version of 
>VMS?

The particular controller you are talking about (the DEQNA) was
de-supported because it was sufficiently broken, and a replacement
(the DELQA) was available so continued DEQNA support wasn't worth the
effort. I wouldn't expect there to be any reason to de-support the
built-in controllers in the VAXstations since 1) they really aren't
broken; and 2) There's no replacement option, until at least the point in
the distant future when/if the whole system is no longer supported.

-Mike



