In article <3664592F.420032EA@nospam.usask.ca>, Chris Pitzel <chris.pitzel@nospam.usask.ca> writes:
> To make a long story short, DEC blamed Seagate's firmware, and Seagate
> blamed DEC for making their operating system specifically reject
> non-DEC-branded drives (DEC branded drives are usually just Seagate
> Barracudas anyways..).

I've found a pretty even mix between the Seagate Barracudas and the Quantum,
formerly DEC, drives. Even a single order for the same DEC part number, say
a hundred RZ1DB-VW results in a mix of drives. The only way you can really
tell is to connect to the HSx controller and SHOW DISK###. Check the last
letter of the drive part number, and the firmware rev level as below:

HSJ0>sho disk640
Name          Type          Port Targ  Lun                    Used by
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DISK640       disk             6    4    0                    D173
          DEC      RZ1DF-CB (C) DEC 0371	<<<Seagate

HSJ0>sho disk630
Name          Type          Port Targ  Lun                    Used by
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DISK630       disk             6    3    0                    D167
          DEC      RZ1CB-CA (C) DEC LYJ0	<<<Quantum

There are some interesting differences in the equivalent drives depending on
your intended use.
                                                                         
	Bob Kaplow	



